<title>USA: US Rep Archer proposes moving tax to Airport Fund.</title>
<headline>US Rep Archer proposes moving tax to Airport Fund.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. House Ways and Means Committee Chairman Bill Archer proposed changes in his tax cut legislation that would earmark funds from an aviation gasoline tax for the Airport and Airway Trust Fund.</p>
<p>Under Archer's original proposal, the 4.3 cents per gallon excise tax on aviation gasoline and jet fuel would have been deposited in the general fund.</p>
<p>The provision would be effective for fuels removed or sold after September 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The Airport and Airway Trust Fund is used to fund airport repairs and improvements and to pay for operations including air traffic controllers.</p>
<p>((-- Washington Newsroom (202) 898-8300))</p>
